file_merger: a backslash-escaped quote inside a quoted CSV field (checkpoint 1)

Sentence: "escape character defaults to doubling the quote (`\"\"`), overrideable via flags".
The checkpoint-4 fixtures that put JSON in CSV cells escape the inner quotes with backslashes
(`"{\"name\":\"ok\"}"`), which RFC 4180 doubling never produces. The min11-ABDFJKMN runs read
those cells as broken JSON and nulled the whole row's nested columns; the reference solution
sniffs the file for `\"` and, finding it, reads with backslash as the escape character.
Tests: correct_aliases/case1, correct_nested/case1, correct_nested/case5, correct_nested/case8
(checkpoint 4).

--- a/file_merger/checkpoint_1.md
+++ b/file_merger/checkpoint_1.md
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@

 - All inputs are UTF-8, RFC-4180 compliant, with a **header row**
 - Delimiter is comma (`,`); line ending `\n`
-- Quote character defaults to `"`; escape character defaults to doubling the quote (`""`), overrideable via flags
+- Quote character defaults to `"`; escape character defaults to doubling the quote (`""`) and accepts backslash-escapes (`\"`), overrideable via flags
 - No multiline fields will be present in tests

